Subject: [PATCH] MilkdropPreset: compensate reference-scale feedback diffusion

Build on 0032 (numbered 0036 after PR #27's 0033-0035; previously 0030) and PR #23's sampler and feedback-history fixes. Add (scale^2-1)/6 render pixels^2
per axis through an exact-moment adaptive 3/4-tap stencil, capped at 1.9, for bilinear warp reads
only. One pass with two render targets writes the exact y-flipped frame and its filtered copy.
Point-sampled warp reads (pw/pc main and aliases, by the bound sampler's filter mode) and the
composite read the exact copy, as at the reference size; encoded state in point-read channels is
not averaged. The pass replaces the required end-of-frame flip and is recomputed before the warp
after new motion vectors, so pass counts match the uncompensated path. Keep the ordinary path
without a reference, at/below its area, for conservatively gated shaders, and after shader failure.

Scale the minimum vector length only with active compensation; invalidate cached
input when scale/reference or framebuffer state changes. Cache uniform locations.
Shader compilation cleanup is provided by prerequisite patch 0025.
WarpSamplerTest's packed point-state and mixed-routing regressions come from 02504a3a's
alternative P1-subset fix on the feature branch; this patch keeps single-pass placement.

The nine-tap PoC (229ae74) missed AM6 cost targets. Independent productisation
measurements and deliberate kernel/placement/routing changes are recorded under
 docs/superpowers/evidence/0025-feedback-diffusion/.
